# Language statistics
#
# GitHub's language bar counts every tracked file, which put this repository at
# roughly half PowerShell. None of that PowerShell is in the application: it is
# all under tools/, and it builds the MSIX, draws the icon, banner and social
# card, captures the demo and encodes the GIF. The program itself is C# and XAML
# with no PowerShell in it at all, so the bar was describing the build tooling
# rather than the thing people download.
#
# linguist-detectable=false is the attribute meant for this. It says "leave these
# out of the statistics" without the dishonesty of linguist-vendored, which would
# claim the scripts are third-party code, or linguist-generated, which would claim
# nothing wrote them by hand. The files stay in the repository, stay syntax
# highlighted, and stay searchable — they simply stop being counted.
#
# Only the scripts are excluded, not all of tools/. tools/BeastClicker.Benchmarks
# is real C# that this project owns and it should keep counting toward the bar.
tools/*.ps1 linguist-detectable=false
